{
 "$comment": "`always` lists must-haves every ad keeps whatever the brief says (the logo: an ad without the brand mark is not an ad of the brand). How `ad` turns a brief into ads: which layouts (image templates and compose recipes) can carry which brief fields, what each suits, and how they rank. The layouts themselves live in image.json, layouts.mjs and recipes.json; restyle those and these entries keep working. `alternates` are other arrangements of a recipe (block options, and cells with `at`), tried after its themes. `fields` maps a brief field to the template's slot or the recipe's block.slot; `pictures` names the picture kinds a layout takes (template: kinds, min, max; recipe: block id to kinds); `needs` are brief fields it cannot draw without; `sizes` limits a layout to those sizes (templates default to their own, recipes to their size list). Every candidate is drawn and checked; one that breaks a rule or stops reading at a size is skipped for the next. Sample copy is the site's own words and Acme only.",
